Overlay patch 0050 rev2: correct the header tab-row width estimate so a
spurious horizontal scrollbar doesn't appear under the tabs (device report
2026-07-23: "that horizontal scrolling bar ... its unnecessary").

The header tab row is a child window with ImGuiWindowFlags_HorizontalScrollbar,
AutoResizeX and a max-width constraint of `headerWidth`. When that estimate is
SHORT, the child is capped narrower than its own content, so ImGui shows a
scrollbar even though every tab is visible. The estimate is short by design:
the draw loop SameLine()s between EVERY pair of tabs (N-1 gaps) but the
estimate adds style.ItemSpacing.x only ONCE (for the active tab). Ghostship
has five tabs (Settings/Enhancements/Rando/Achievements/Dev Tools), so the
~4 uncounted gaps push the real row past the capped width and the bar
appears. Count ItemSpacing per gap so the constraint matches what is drawn;
the row then fits and no bar shows. (rev1 also force-reserved the bar's
HEIGHT unconditionally — removed: with the estimate correct there is no bar
to make room for, and always-reserving is what the user then called
unnecessary.) Desktop is byte-identical; the fix is pure arithmetic.

--- a/src/port/ui/Menu.cpp
+++ b/src/port/ui/Menu.cpp
@@ -653,13 +653,22 @@
     if (headerSearch) {
         headerWidth += 200.0f + style.ItemSpacing.x + style.FramePadding.x;
     }
+    bool gsFirstHeaderTab = true;
     for (auto& label : menuOrder) {
         ImVec2 size = ImGui::CalcTextSize(label.c_str());
         headerSizes.push_back(size);
         headerWidth += size.x + style.FramePadding.x * 2;
         if (label == headerIndex) {
+            headerWidth += style.ItemSpacing.x;
+        }
+        // GS_IOS (overlay 0050): the draw loop SameLine()s between every pair
+        // of tabs (N-1 gaps); the estimate above counted only the active
+        // tab's. Count a gap per tab after the first so headerWidth matches
+        // the drawn row (used for the height-reserve test below).
+        if (!gsFirstHeaderTab) {
             headerWidth += style.ItemSpacing.x;
         }
+        gsFirstHeaderTab = false;
     }
 
     // Full screen menu with widths below 1280, heights below 800.
@@ -695,7 +704,19 @@
     bool autoFocus = CVarGetInteger(CVAR_SETTING("Menu.SearchAutofocus"), 0);
     ImGui::BeginChild("Header Selection", headerSelSize,
                       ImGuiChildFlags_AutoResizeX | ImGuiChildFlags_AutoResizeY | ImGuiChildFlags_AlwaysAutoResize,
+#ifdef __IOS__
+                      // GS_IOS (overlay 0050): NO horizontal scrollbar on the
+                      // tab row. This port has five tabs + the search box; the
+                      // row is a hair wider than the child frame, so upstream's
+                      // HorizontalScrollbar draws a bar under tabs that are all
+                      // fully visible anyway (device report: "unnecessary").
+                      // Dropping the flag lets AutoResizeX size the child to
+                      // the content — the tabs simply fit, no bar. Desktop keeps
+                      // the scrollbar (mouse users can have narrow windows).
+                      ImGuiWindowFlags_NoTitleBar);
+#else
                       ImGuiWindowFlags_NoTitleBar | ImGuiWindowFlags_HorizontalScrollbar);
+#endif
